{"nodes": [{"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_daily_log", "label": "2026-09-14 Tasks Completed Log", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_athlete_invitations_page_redesign", "label": "Athlete Invitations Page Redesign", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Old page read as novice work \u2014 no search, weak hierarchy, spec jargon in user-facing copy. Redesigned to the marketplace's visual language while staying a pure server component (search via GET ?q=, stat strip, urgency-sorted cards, \u00a7 references removed from copy)."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_athlete_earnings_page_redesign", "label": "Athlete Earnings Page Redesign", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Old page taught the \u00a721 state machine instead of answering the athlete's questions; redesigned around reading order (how much have I made \u2192 what's arriving \u2192 where is each dollar \u2192 is anything stuck). Iterated from no-JS toolbar/details to one client island by explicit user preference \u2014 the no-JS rule gave way to UX."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_activity_explorer", "label": "ActivityExplorer client island (src/components/activity-explorer.tsx)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replaced the Apply-button/details-accordion no-JS approach the user found clunky: instant filtering, slide-over drawer, custom Dropdown and DateRangePicker popovers, filter-chips row."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_earnings_ui", "label": "Earnings UI shared copy module (src/lib/earnings-ui.ts)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shared copy (EARNING_TONE, JOURNEY, STAGE_INDEX, STATUS_DETAIL, STATE_ORDER, MONTHS) imported by both the server page and the client island so stage language can't drift."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_url_param_state_pattern", "label": "URL-param state house pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "House pattern of URL-param state everywhere: plain GET forms and links carry q/state/demo params so URLs stay shareable with zero client JS."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_replacestate_url_sync_idiom", "label": "history.replaceState URL-sync idiom", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Client-island filter/tab state syncs to the URL via history.replaceState (no navigation) and the server page seeds it back from searchParams, so filtered/deep-linked views stay shareable and SSR correctly; stale params degrade to defaults."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_slide_over_drawer", "label": "Slide-over drawer pattern (sx-drawer choreography)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Right-side drawer portaled to document.body with sx-drawer/sx-backdrop keyframes, staggered content entrance, animated close waiting on animationend with a fallback unmount timer, Escape/backdrop close, focus management, reduced-motion durations of 1ms (not none) so close events still fire."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_sx_animate_portal_gotcha", "label": "sx-animate ancestor transform gotcha", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "sx-animate (fill-mode: both) leaves a transform on the ancestor section, making it the containing block for position: fixed, so full-screen overlays get clipped to the section. Any overlay rendered under an sx-animate ancestor must portal out to document.body (createPortal, SSR-safe when render is click-gated)."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_no_backdrop_filter_lesson", "label": "No full-viewport backdrop-filter on overlays", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "backdrop-blur-[2px] on a full-viewport backdrop janks the main thread exactly when the close click needs processing (827\u2013943ms click paths vs 320ms Escape). Removing the blur (bg-black/55 instead) cut backdrop-click close to 344ms."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_filter_chips_row", "label": "Filter-chips row pattern", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "User rejected the icon-only reset button; of four offered options chose dismissible per-filter chips below the toolbar plus a quiet Clear-all and right-aligned result count. Removing one chip cleans only that URL param."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_athlete_profile_ux_pass", "label": "Athlete Profile UX Pass (no portal \u2192 public context switch)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The sidebar's Public profile item jumped athletes out of the portal to the public marketing site with dead tabs and an inert Follow button. Replaced with an in-portal owner view; /athletes/[slug]?from=athlete-portal now redirects to /athlete/profile so stale bookmarks can't strand an athlete on the public surface."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_athlete_profile_preview_page", "label": "Athlete portal profile page (src/app/(app)/athlete/profile/page.tsx)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In-portal owner view of the public profile with 'This is you' chip, Invitations pointer instead of Request Partnership, profile-completion nudge (72% Meter), and 'Open public page \u2197' as the one explicit exit."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_athlete_profile_view", "label": "AthleteProfileView shared component (src/components/athlete-profile-view.tsx)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Client component shared by the public page and the owner view: real accessible tabs (roving focus, ?tab= deep links), owner vs public variants, only ever touches athletePublic so the sponsor-price-only rule (\u00a704/\u00a730) holds."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_public_athlete_profile_page", "label": "Public athlete profile page (src/app/(public)/athletes/[slug]/page.tsx)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Thin server wrapper: resolveBack + BackLink plus a 'PUBLIC PROFILE \u00b7 VISIBLE TO ANYONE' orientation label so portal users always know which surface they're on."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_owner_framed_self_view_lesson", "label": "Owner-framed self-view lesson", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A portal-embedded view of a public page should be framed for its owner (self-view), not as a pixel-faithful sponsor preview \u2014 inert sponsor-side buttons (Follow, Request Partnership on your own profile) confuse more than they inform."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_profile_sections", "label": "Profile sections data module (src/lib/profile-sections.ts)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The nine \u00a711 sections as shared data (key, label, public/private scope, blurb) plus a checklist-label \u2192 section-key map; server-safe so pages can deep-link without importing the client island."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_profile_editor", "label": "ProfileEditor client island (src/components/profile-editor.tsx)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fixture-backed edit prototype built ahead of the blocked backend (P3-BE-01/05, P3-FE-01/03). A hub, not a wizard \u2014 editing is random-access. Every pane carries a Public/Private scope chip because 'who sees this?' is the first athlete question; saves flash 'queued for BTG review' (managed-marketplace semantics, \u00a710); payment pane repeats the no-bank-details/no-tax-ID rule (\u00a726/A6)."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_athlete_profile_edit_page", "label": "Athlete profile edit page (src/app/(app)/athlete/profile/edit/page.tsx)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Portal page hosting the editor: BTG-review notice banner, 'edits live in this tab only' honesty, seeds ?section= from searchParams."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_admin_applications_page_redesign", "label": "Admin Applications Page Redesign", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Old page was a flat dump of every application fully expanded with spec jargon and dead title-attribute-only buttons. Redesigned as a review desk on the earnings-page idioms: hero band with aging alert (AGING_HOURS = 48), one client island, review drawer with pinned decision bar, locally-applied decisions with Undo."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_filter_kit", "label": "FilterKit shared controls (src/components/filter-kit.tsx)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SearchInput, Dropdown, FilterChip, useOutsideClose, trigger/panel classes and shared icons extracted out of activity-explorer and made tone-aware ('athlete' | 'admin' static class maps) so both portals reuse the same designed controls."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_use_outside_close", "label": "useOutsideClose hook", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Playwright found outside-click dismissal clicked through to the activity row beneath and opened the drawer; the hook now swallows the click that follows the closing pointerdown (capture-phase, once). Accepted cost: switching triggers while a popover is open takes two clicks."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_applications_ui", "label": "Applications UI copy module (src/lib/applications-ui.ts)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Server-safe shared copy: STATE_TONE/STATE_DETAIL, scoreBand() (\u226570 Strong / \u226555 Solid / \u226540 Developing / <40 Weak fit), FACTOR_HINTS (plain-English line per \u00a714 factor), waitHours parser."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_applications_desk", "label": "ApplicationsDesk client island (src/components/applications-desk.tsx)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The admin applications page's one island: tabs with live counts, instant search, attention/sort dropdowns, ScoreRing per row, review drawer with pinned decision bar, and locally-applied Approve/Request-info/Reject decisions with Undo (Follow-button precedent); a minor with an unverified guardian gets a warn strip explaining the \u00a74 lock instead of a dead button."}, {"id": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_score_ring", "label": "ScoreRing component", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The \u00a714 score as an SVG ring that sweeps in on mount (stroke-dashoffset transition, motion-reduce:transition-none), colored by score band; replaced the old separate score-distribution card."}], "edges": [{"source": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_daily_log", "target": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_athlete_invitations_page_redesign", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_daily_log", "target": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_athlete_earnings_page_redesign", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_daily_log", "target": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_athlete_profile_ux_pass", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_daily_log", "target": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_admin_applications_page_redesign", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_athlete_invitations_page_redesign", "target": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_url_param_state_pattern", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_athlete_earnings_page_redesign", "target": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_activity_explorer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Memory/2026-09-14/tasks-completed.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "memory_2026_09_14_tasks_completed_athlete_earnings_page_redesign", "target": "